  "contract": "browser-corpus-byte-batch-mixed-materialization-headroom-matrix",
  "note": "This is a browser-runtime counterexample search over Uint8Array batches. Variant memory is browser JS heap; host process-tree memory is reported separately when available.",
  "sourceContract": {
    "parserInput": "Prepared full rows use StreamReaderSync over a synchronous Iterable<Uint8Array[]> generated by byteBatches(fixture); live fetch rows consume Response.body either through EventReader or manually grouped AsyncIterable<Uint8Array[]> batches.",
    "batchBackpressure": "byteBatches(fixture) yields one grouped batch per synchronous parser pull. fetchAsyncByteBatchFull groups Response.body with reader.read() only while filling the next yielded Uint8Array[] batch, so it is demand-driven and does not eagerly drain the stream.",
    "fetchReadableStream": "fetchReadableStreamFull consumes fetch Response.body directly with EventReader while the local server repeats corpus bytes to the target size; fetchAsyncByteBatchFull manually groups Response.body reads into AsyncIterable<Uint8Array[]> batches under the same contract.",
    "corpusScope": "Most corpus rows still load fetch(...).arrayBuffer() as a seed and replay it; fetchReadableStreamFull and fetchAsyncByteBatchFull are live browser streaming source rows."
  },
